    {
      "id": "iZjOYuyd45cPn0uNqxaOe",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1493.9961441778862,
      "y": 1252.2295553407027,
      "width": 783.759521484375,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0K",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1171705434,
      "version": 105,
      "versionNonce": 1596485190,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1782235183144,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "I would not mutate investor state directly inside the webhook handler. I would\ntreat webhooks as unreliable external events: verify with raw body, durably\npersist before ACK, dedupe with durable constraints, process asynchronously,\nnormalize through provider adapters, reconcile critical terminal events with\nprovider APIs, then signal a Temporal workflow that owns the onboarding state\nmachine.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "I would not mutate investor state directly inside the webhook handler. I would treat webhooks as unreliable external events: verify with raw body, durably persist before ACK, dedupe with durable constraints, process asynchronously, normalize through provider adapters, reconcile critical terminal events with provider APIs, then signal a Temporal workflow that owns the onboarding state machine.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
